    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0207" n="195" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg195"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.0146/298</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3831</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-08">March 8, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit herewith a copy of a
                        letter<anchor n="32" xml:id="d104-f1"/> from General Hilldring<anchor n="33"
                        xml:id="d104-f2"/> and a copy of the enclosure thereto which it is believed
                    are self-explanatory. It will be observed that the memorandum from the Joint
                    Chiefs of Staff delineates the zones to be occupied in Germany by American,
                    British, and Soviet forces and that it was prepared on December 4, 1943. This
                    document is transmitted to you for your consideration and for your
                    recommendations with regard to it.</p>
                <p>There are also enclosed herewith (1) a map setting forth the Soviet proposal
                    concerning zones; (2) a map setting forth the United States Joint Chiefs of
                    Staff proposal; and (3) a cartogram comparing maps one <pb facs="0208" n="196"
                        xml:id="pg196"/> and two.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d104-f3"/> These maps were
                    prepared in the Department as of possible assistance to you.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward</hi> R. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stettinius, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d104-a1.xml" xpointer="d104-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d104-f1" n="32" xml:id="d104-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d104-f2" n="33" xml:id="d104-f2-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. John H. Hilldring, Director of the Civil Affairs Division of the War
                    Department.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d104-f3" n="34" xml:id="d104-f3-content">
                <p>The three enclosures were not found attached to the file copy of this document.
                    Copies of the two maps and the cartogram (reproduced on facing page) are
                    included in the EAC files: Lot 52 M 64, box 9602, files 136 and 138
                    Germany—Zones of Occupation I.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
